// 003.15 (D36, #39, #40, #14): `Role ... Is ...`, status facts as actors, `Except` in quantifiers,
// fixed duty claimants, ordered succession `First of ... Unless`, `%` on `Duration`, and `Var`
// projection over an enumerated domain.
Fact person Identified by Helen, Marcus, Asha, Luis, Mei, Daniel, Priya
Role principal Is Helen
Role agent Is Marcus
Fact reported Identified by agent
Duty report-due Holder agent Claimant Helen Created by deal
Power deal Actor agent Recipient person Valid when True Creates reported(agent)

Fact roommate Identified by person
Fact approved Identified by person * person'
Act approve-candidate Actor roommate Related to person' Holds when True Creates approved(roommate, person')

Var rent-payer Identified by person
Fact owes-payer Identified by person * person'
  Derived from (Foreach roommate: owes-payer(roommate.person, rent-payer.person)
    When roommate.person != rent-payer.person)

Fact unavailable Identified by person
Role executor For person First of Daniel, Priya Unless unavailable(person)
Bool estate-closed
Power close-estate Actor executor Valid when True Creates estate-closed()

Param epoch : Time = 0
Bool daniel-week Holds when ((Current Time - epoch) % 14) < 7
.
// 1. Role agent Is Marcus: Helen cannot validly exercise `deal`; Marcus can, and creates `report-due(Marcus, Helen)`!
?!valid deal(Helen, Asha).
?valid deal(Marcus, Asha).
deal(Marcus, Asha).
?report-due(Marcus, Helen).

// 2. Status fact as actor + `Forall ... Except`:
+roommate(Asha). +roommate(Luis).
?!valid approve-candidate(Mei, Priya).
?valid approve-candidate(Asha, Priya).
approve-candidate(Asha, Priya).
?(Forall roommate Except Luis: approved(roommate, Priya)).

// 3. Var projection over enumerated type (`#14`): only Asha is `rent-payer`, never Mei!
+rent-payer(Asha).
?owes-payer(Luis, Asha).
?!owes-payer(Luis, Mei).

// 4. Ordered succession (`First of Daniel, Priya Unless unavailable(person)`):
?valid close-estate(Daniel).
?!valid close-estate(Priya).
+unavailable(Daniel).
?!valid close-estate(Daniel).
?valid close-estate(Priya).

// 5. Alternating turns via `%` on `Duration`:
?daniel-week().
@ 8.
?!daniel-week().
@ 15.
?daniel-week().
